{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB06595 - MONDO_5224",
  "verbalization": "Midostaurin is associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation through a chain of indications that link the drug to a subset of acute myeloid leukemia (AML) cases. The evidence suggests that Midostaurin is indicated for Acute Myeloid Leukemia With Minimal Differentiation, which in turn is linked to Tioguanine and Ivosidenib, both of which are indicated for Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation. This implies that Midostaurin may exert its therapeutic effect through a mechanism that is broadly applicable to a subset of AML cases, potentially through the modulation of cellular pathways or epigenetic regulation. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to the same final target—Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation—suggests a possible role in the treatment of this subset, possibly through the inhibition of specific molecular targets or the enhancement of cellular responses to treatment. The integration of these indications highlights the potential for Midostaurin to be repurposed in the management of this disease, though further mechanistic studies are needed to clarify the exact relationship and the underlying pathways involved.",
